            <ArticleTitle>The cost of compensable low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cost data were retrieved from all claims of low back pain initiated during 1986 (N = 98,999) from computerized records of the Liberty Mutual Insurance Company. The mean cost per case was $6807; median cost, $391. Medical costs represented 31.5% of the total costs; indemnity costs, 67.2%. The total compensable cost for all low back pain in the United States was estimated to be $11.1 billion. Large variations were found to exist among different states in cost per case and percentage of costs for indemnity and medical payments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
